Finding: {"title":"idempotency_keys table has no tenant scoping — global key namespace across all flight schools","severity":"MEDIUM","area":"Idempotency / tenant isolation","files":["src/lib/idempotency.ts","drizzle/0142_add_idempotency_keys.sql"],"detail":"The idempotency_keys table (drizzle/0142) has PK key varchar(255) with no flight_school_id/tenant column, and withIdempotency() (src/lib/idempotency.ts:9) looks up/stores purely by the caller-supplied key string with no tenant qualifier. If any caller derives the idempotency key from client-controllable or non-globally-unique input, one flight school's request could collide with another's key and receive a cached response containing a different tenant's data.","impact":"Cross-tenant response leakage if two different flight schools' requests ever produce the same idempotency key. Currently zero callers found for withIdempotency( outside its own definition, so not yet exploitable, but it is landmine dead code waiting for the first caller.","recommendation":"Add a flight_school_id column to idempotency_keys, include it in the lookup/insert WHERE and uniqueness constraint, and require callers to pass the tenant id explicitly. Compare to accounting_provider_idempotency_keys (drizzle/0346) which correctly scopes by owner_type, owner_id, provider, ... — follow that pattern.","confidence":"medium"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

